 "about_text": "L.A. Louver is a contemporary art gallery in Venice, California, founded in 1975 by Peter and Elizabeth Goulds. It opened to the public on North Venice Boulevard in 1976 with a mission to place Southern California artists in an international context while bringing global artists to Los Angeles audiences. Over five decades the gallery has represented a roster of established postwar and contemporary painters and sculptors, mounting hundreds of exhibitions and building an extensive archive documenting its history and artists' records. Its program spans painting, sculpture, assemblage, ceramics, and works on paper, with a strong emphasis on figuration, abstraction, and cross-generational dialogue between Los Angeles and international artists.",
